   "subject": "Re: Question about suitable buffer width",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div>Erica</div><div>I assume you have seen <a href=\"https://www.otago.ac.nz/density/pdfs/secr-habitatmasks.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.otago.ac.nz/density/pdfs/secr-habitatmasks.pdf&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792486393593000&amp;usg=AOvVaw15eoKmLbTd9BW_LmnsgrCD\">secr-habitatmasks.pdf</a> and tried esa.plot() (much faster than repeated fits). Is there a reason you resist using 8 km? What is your basis for thinking it&#39;s way too large? Why is 4 km sensible and 8 km not? Are there some extreme movements (possibly data errors) that might be inflating estimates of sigma? You can see it&#39;s hard for us to address the question...</div>Murray"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"auto\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Monday, February 19, 2024 at 1:26:14 PM UTC+13 <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ericahe...@gmail.com</a> wrote:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><p style=\"color:rgb(36,36,36);font-size:15px;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"><span style=\"border:0px;font-variant:inherit;font-weight:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;font-size:11pt;line-height:inherit;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;font-kerning:inherit;font-feature-settings:inherit;margin:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline\">Hi all,</span></p><p style=\"color:rgb(36,36,36);font-size:15px;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"><span style=\"border:0px;font-variant:inherit;font-weight:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;font-size:11pt;line-height:inherit;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;font-kerning:inherit;font-feature-settings:inherit;margin:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline\"><br></span></p><p style=\"color:rgb(36,36,36);font-size:15px;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"><span style=\"border:0px;font-variant:inherit;font-weight:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;font-size:11pt;line-height:inherit;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;font-kerning:inherit;font-feature-settings:inherit;margin:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline\">I have been analysing some camera trapping data using secr for the first time, with a mark-resight model, and am unsure about my choice of buffer. I understand that the density should reach an asymptote with increasing buffer width, and by running the model multiple times with different buffer widths, I can see this happening. However, the density only levels out at around 8km, which seems way too large for what we know about the home ranges/movements of these animals. I&#39;d expect a sensible buffer to be about 4km. </span></p><p style=\"color:rgb(36,36,36);font-size:15px;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"><span style=\"border:0px;font-variant:inherit;font-weight:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;font-size:11pt;line-height:inherit;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;font-kerning:inherit;font-feature-settings:inherit;margin:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline\"><br aria-hidden=\"true\"></span></p><p style=\"color:rgb(36,36,36);font-size:15px;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"><span style=\"border:0px;font-variant:inherit;font-weight:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;font-size:11pt;line-height:inherit;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;font-kerning:inherit;font-feature-settings:inherit;margin:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline\">I tried comparing the hazard function vs. half-normal but these gave similar results. I am not sure what to try next, or whether to leave the buffer at 4km or 8km. Any ideas would be welcome. I&#39;m new to this type of analysis so this might be a simple issue!</span></p><p style=\"color:rgb(36,36,36);font-size:15px;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"><span style=\"border:0px;font-variant:inherit;font-weight:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;font-size:11pt;line-height:inherit;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;font-kerning:inherit;font-feature-settings:inherit;margin:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline\"><br></span></p><p style=\"color:rgb(36,36,36);font-size:15px;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"><span style=\"border:0px;font-variant:inherit;font-weight:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;font-size:11pt;line-height:inherit;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;font-kerning:inherit;font-feature-settings:inherit;margin:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline\">Many thanks,</span></p><p style=\"color:rgb(36,36,36);font-size:15px;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"><span style=\"border:0px;font-variant:inherit;font-weight:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;font-size:11pt;line-height:inherit;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;font-kerning:inherit;font-feature-settings:inherit;margin:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline\">Erica</span></p><p style=\"color:rgb(36,36,36);font-size:15px;margin-top:0px;margin-b